# Archive folders - prevent accidental commits of superseded CODE.
# These patterns are deliberately broad, and until 2026-09-16 they silently swallowed the
# DOCUMENTATION archives too: a fresh clone got none of the original requirements set even
# though the docs tree itself was tracked. The re-includes below fix that.
# NOTE: git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded, so each negation
# must name the directory itself - do not "simplify" these into a file glob.
*/archive/
**/Archive/
!docs2/archive/
!GCCWebApp/docs/Final Req Docs/archive/
!GCCWebApp/docs/OneDrive_2026-05-09/Final Req Docs/archive/
pages_old/
Archive_GCCWebApp.Tests/
GCCWebApp-Tests/

# Development session files
nul
updates_*.txt
SecurityUpdates_*.txt
SecurityandPenTesting_*.txt
issuesList*.txt
documentupdates.txt
apiUpdates.txt

# Environment variables and secrets - NEVER commit to source control
.env
.env.local
.env.development
.env.production
.env.staging
*.env
!.env.example
/0_Documentation/00 GCC_ImplementationDocuments_8_22_25/GCC Wireframes_UserStories_8_25_25.pptx
/GCCWebApp/.claude/settings.local.json
/GCCWebApp/deploy-fresh
/GCCWebApp/deploy-out
/GCCWebApp/deploy-staging-20260504-1657
/GCCWebApp/deploy-staging-20260504-1815
/GCCWebApp/publish-20260504-2301
# /GCCWebApp/Database_Scripts - UN-IGNORED 2026-09-16. These are hand-run DB fix scripts
# referenced by the defect register; six were already tracked (added before this rule), so the
# rule only ever hid the newest two, which is the worst of both worlds.
/GCCWebApp/docs/tracking/client-exec-brief-qc-volume-5-13.docx

# DEF-263: server-only secrets overlay. Holds the SMTP mailbox password (and any
# future runtime secret) on the deployed box ONLY. Never commit it, and never let
# it into a deploy zip - Scripts/deploy.ps1 aborts if it reaches staging.
appsettings.Secrets.json
**/appsettings.Secrets.json

# Migration run artifacts. Each dated folder is a full regenerable dump of the
# client dataset (~3-6 MB of generated SQL per run, ~2.8 MB of CSV per run) and
# there is one per re-run, so committing them grows the repo by tens of MB for
# output the scripts reproduce from the source workbooks. The generators are
# tracked; their output is not. Earlier dated folders committed before
# 2026-08-21 stay tracked - .gitignore does not untrack them.
/GCCWebApp/Scripts/data-ops/_sql_output/
/GCCWebApp/Scripts/data-ops/_transform_output/
# Raw DB dumps that feed the spreadsheet-to-database verifier; re-dumped by
# 2026-08-15-verify-dump.ps1 / 2026-08-18-asin-reconciliation-dump.ps1.
/GCCWebApp/Scripts/data-ops/_verify_input/

# dotnet run stderr capture from local dev
_dev.log.err
